{{smaller block|Out of patience with the whole tribe of custom-house extortioners, boatmen, tide-waiters, and ''water-bailifs'', that beset me on all sides, worse than a swarm of musquetoes, I proceeded a little too roughly to brush them away with my rattan.
{{right|''Cumberland'', West Indian, i. 5.}}}}

